/-!
# The higher-codimension Gysin formula for a class satisfying the regular formula

Let `(S, δ)` be as in Stacks 02QL, let `i : Z ⟶ X` be a closed immersion of schemes locally of
finite type over `S` with a virtual normal sheaf `𝒩` locally free of rank `r`, and let `Y ⟶ X` be
locally of finite type. **Stacks 0FEA** asserts that if

1. `𝒩` is locally free of rank `r`,
2. every irreducible component of `Y` has `δ`-dimension `n`,
3. `dim_δ(Z ×_X Y) ≤ n - r`, and
4. for every `ξ ∈ Z ×_X Y` with `δ(ξ) = n - r` the local ring `𝒪_{Y, ξ}` is Cohen–Macaulay,

then `c(Z ⟶ X, 𝒩) ∩ [Y]_n = [Z ×_X Y]_{n - r}`.

The source's proof uses two facts about the class `c = c(Z ⟶ X, 𝒩)`: that it is a bivariant
class of degree `r`, and the excess intersection formula of Stacks 0FBM at vanishing excess,
`c ∩ [V]_n = [Z ×_X V]_{n - r}` whenever `Z ×_X V ⟶ V` is a regular closed immersion of
codimension `r`. This module proves the lemma for every bivariant class `c ∈ A^r(Z ⟶ X)` with that
second property, `Stacks.Chow.BivariantClass.CapRegularFormula`, under the four hypotheses of the
source, with hypothesis (1) in the source's form. The rest of the proof is the source's:

* at a point `ξ ∈ Z ×_X Y` of `δ`-dimension `n - r` the local ring `𝒪_{Y, ξ}` has dimension `r`
  by (2), the ideal of `Z ×_X Y` in it is generated by `r` elements by (1), and it is an ideal of
  definition by (3); by (4) and Algebra, Lemma 10.104.2 (Stacks 02JN) it is generated by a regular
  sequence (`Stacks.Chow.isRegular_of_isCohenMacaulayLocalRing_stalk`, in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.BivariantLemmas.VirtualNormalCapFundamental`);
* by Divisors, Lemma 31.20.6 (Stacks 063I) that sequence cuts out `Z ×_X Y` over an open
  neighbourhood `V` of `ξ` in `Y`, on which `Z ×_X V ⟶ V` is a regular closed immersion of
  codimension `r`, so the formula holds over `V`;
* restriction to `V` commutes with the cap product (Stacks 0B76) and carries fundamental classes
  to fundamental classes, and by (3) `CH_{n-r}(Z ×_X Y)` is the group of `(n-r)`-cycles, so a class
  in it is determined by its restrictions to neighbourhoods of the points of `δ`-dimension `n - r`.

Stacks 0FEA itself, for the class `c(Z ⟶ X, 𝒩)`, is in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.BivariantLemmas.VirtualNormalCapCohenMacaulay`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.BivariantClass.CapRegularFormula` — the formula
  `c ∩ [V]_n = [Z ×_X V]_{n - r}` over every base change `V` pure of `δ`-dimension `n` on which
  `Z ×_X V ⟶ V` is a regular closed immersion of codimension `r`; for `c(Z ⟶ X, 𝒩)` this is Stacks
  0FBM at vanishing excess.
* `Stacks.Chow.BivariantClass.CapCohenMacaulayFormula` — the conclusion of Stacks 0FEA under
  (2)–(4), as a property of a class of any morphism.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.exists_isRegularClosedImmersionOfCodim_of_isRegular_stalk` — a closed immersion
  cut out at a point by a regular sequence of length `r` is a regular closed immersion of
  codimension `r` over a neighbourhood of that point (Stacks 063I).
* `Stacks.Chow.deltaDimension_irreducibleComponents_of_isOpenImmersion` — a scheme open in a
  scheme pure of `δ`-dimension `n` is pure of `δ`-dimension `n`.
* `Stacks.Chow.BivariantClass.cap_fundamentalChowClass_eq_of_generators` — the lemma with
  hypothesis (1) replaced by its consequence that the ideal of `Z ×_X Y` is generated by `r`
  elements at the points of `δ`-dimension `n - r`.
* `Stacks.Chow.BivariantClass.cap_fundamentalChowClass_eq_of_capRegularFormula` — the lemma for
  every bivariant class of degree `r` satisfying the formula: under (1)–(4),
  `c ∩ [Y]_n = [Z ×_X Y]_{n - r}`.
* `Stacks.Chow.BivariantClass.capCohenMacaulayFormula_of_capRegularFormula` — the same, as an
  implication between the two properties, for a closed immersion with a virtual normal sheaf of
  rank `r`.

## Implementation notes

**The class.** The proof is written for an arbitrary bivariant class `c ∈ A^r(Z ⟶ X)` satisfying
`Stacks.Chow.BivariantClass.CapRegularFormula`, which is the only property of the class it uses
besides bivariance; the class `c(Z ⟶ X, 𝒩)` of Stacks 0FBK satisfies the formula by Stacks 0FBM
at vanishing excess, once the conormal sheaf of a regular closed immersion of codimension `r` is
known to have rank `r` (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf`
`.IsRegularClosedImmersionOfCodim.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_conormalSheaf`). The formula is
not the conclusion, since it is asked only of base changes on which `Z ×_X V ⟶ V` is regular of
codimension `r`, while the lemma concerns a `Y` on which `Z ×_X Y ⟶ Y` need not be regular
anywhere outside the points of `δ`-dimension `n - r`. The formula carries the bound
`dim_δ(Z ×_X V) ≤ n - r` among its hypotheses; in the source it follows from the other two.

**Hypothesis (1).** Local freeness of rank `r` enters only through the surjection
`𝒩^∨ ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X}` of Stacks 0FBQ: the kernel of `𝒪_{X, i z} ⟶ 𝒪_{Z, z}` is generated by `r` elements
(`Stacks.Chow.VirtualNormalBundle.exists_ofList_eq_ker_stalkMap`), and its extension to
`𝒪_{Y, y}` is the ideal of `Z ×_X Y` (`Stacks.Chow.exists_ofList_eq_ker_stalkMap_pullback_snd`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FEA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FEA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02JN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02JN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B76](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B76)
